@parties
go-to: menu
set-bg: img/neorevs.jpg
face-image: img/VoteSocDem.jpg

<span style="color: #ED1B34;">**RSDRP(O)**</span> - *Rossijskaja Social-Demokratičeskaja Rabočaja Partija (Ob’jedinjonnaja)* (Russian Social Democratic Labour Party (United)) - this is us. We are a socialist and democratic party of the working class. We are the heirs of the legacy of Marx and Engels, Martov and Plekhanov. We are the foremost defenders of the Republic. The modern RSDRP(O) is the continuation of the Menshevik sections of the RSDRP.

<span style="color: #b4121a;">**PSR**</span> - *Pártiya Sotsialístov-Revolyutsionérov* (Party of Socialists-Revolutionaries) - a left-populist, Narodist party that supports the Republic, and has historically supported many of our labor, welfare, and anti-militarist priorities. They have often been in coalitions with us. [? if year >= 1930 or chancellor = "Brüning" : They have appeared to take a more conservative turn recently, with the rise of Brüning and the party leader, Ludwig Kaas. ?]

Current relations: [+ z_relation : relationships +]

# TODO: replace this with the german state party after 1930
<span style="color: #0087dc;">**K-D**</span> - *Konstitutsionno-Demokraticheskaya Partiya/Pártiya Naródnoy Svobódy* (Constitutional Democratic Party, or officially the Party of People's Freedom) - a centrist to center-right liberal party, popular among the intelligensia and educated middle class. They have historically been cordial with us but, especially following their recent conservative turn, oppose our economic policies. The <span style="color: #008000;">**Alash Party**</span> is closely tied to the Kadets, generally considered to be their sister-party in Russian Central Asia. [? if year >= 1930 : They have recently reformed themselves as the German State Party (DStP). ?]

Current relations: [+ ddp_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #004090;">**VS**</span> - *Vserossiyskiy Soyuz* (All-Russian Union) - a conservative, nationalist, and often monarchist party, supported by the middle classes and rural conservatives. They despise us.

Current relations: [+ dnvp_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #3bb9ff;">**Müsavat Party**</span> - *Müsavat Firqəsi* (Müsavat Party) - a pan-Muslim liberal party, with pan-Turkist, conservative, and even Socialist elements. It is supported by a broad coalition of Muslims, from left to right. We have entered coalition talks with them before, though they led to nowhere.

Current relations: [+ dvp_relation : relationships +]

<span style="color: #990000;">**PLSRI**</span> - *Partiya Levykh Sotsialistov-Revolyutsionerov-Internatsionalistov* (Party of Left Socialist-Revolutionaries-Internationalists) - a radical left-wing offshoot of the PSR that emerged in the aftermath of the Civil War, they are split between former Bolsheviks and Narodists. The party is currently crippled by internal fighting, which is unlikely to end soon. 

Current relations: [+ kpd_relation : relationships +]

[? if sapd_formed: <span style="color: #d84c4c;">**SRPR**</span> - *Sotsialisticheskaya Rabočaja partiya* (Socialist Worker's Party of Russia) - a party recently formed in a split from the RSDRP(O), the SRPR is essentially an agglomeration of various left-wing splinter groups between the RSRDP(O) and PLSRI. ?]

<span style="color: #F9DA00;">**NTS**</span> - *Narodno-trudovoy Soyuz Rossiyskikh Solidaristov* - (National Alliance of Russian Solidarists, or Solidarists) - a far-right ultranationalist, corporatist, and reactionary party. Led by Duke Sergei Nikolaevich Leuchtenberg, many of their members and leaders supported monarchist and nationalist groups in the Civil War.

Current relations: [+ nsdap_relation : relationships +]

**Other parties** - there is a multitude of small, mostly conservative, regionalist, or socialist parties, such as the Labourist Popular-Socialist Party, the Armenian Populist Party, the All-Peasant Union, and others. Their political position usually lies between the RSDRP and K-D.

